ealth issue. [Data: Entities (169, 142); Relationships (162, 151)]\n\n## Complications associated with diabetes\n\nDiabetes Mellitus is associated with various complications, including malnutrition, acute pancreatitis, and other chronic conditions. These complications can complicate treatment plans and require coordinated efforts in patient management. Understanding these relationships is crucial for healthcare providers to develop comprehensive care strategies for diabetic patients. [Data: Entities (71, 115); Relationships (170, 186)]\n\n## The role of geriatric residences in diabetes management\n\nGeriatric residences provide specialized care for elderly patients with diabetes, focusing on their unique health and nutritional needs. These facilities play a critical role in managing diabetes among older adults, who are often at higher risk for complications. The relationship between diabetes and geriatric care emphasizes the need for tailored approaches in managing chronic conditions in aging populations. [Data: Entities (144); Relationships (153)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n143,HOSPITAL,\"The hospital is a comprehensive healthcare institution that provides a wide range of medical services and treatments to patients. It is where individuals receive medical attention for various conditions, including consultations in endocrinology and nutrition, as well as surgical and medical treatments. The hospital plays a crucial role in the management of serious illnesses, such as adenocarcinoma of the pancreas, where it facilitates patient admissions and palliative care. Additionally, it offers specialized care for patients with neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's, and supports those with metabolic disorders like diabetes and malnutrition. The hospital is also equipped to provide multidisciplinary care for patients with Mitochondrial Neurogastrointestinal Encephalomyopathy (MNGIE), which includes nutritional support 